' Sizes of the replay authority charges (DR-79, cap root cause C14).
' One replay publication: prepare reserves every charge under the authority
' lock, mutates the reserved ledger and the pending map, and the same
' synchronous window publishes or aborts. Each charge group is sized by the
' maps it searches, after the operation for the deferred publish and abort
' searches. Native execution serializes each frontier (footprint key [2, 0]),
' so the live sizes are a function of the canonical execution.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-79);
'                  rholang/src/rust/interpreter/accounting/native_runtime/
'                  replay_authority/backing.rs (tree_update, reserve_event_lookup,
'                  reserve_changes); replay_authority.rs (prepare, publish, Drop).
' Formal model:    formal/rocq/cost_accounted_rho/theories/OrderedLookupBound.v
'                  (search_within_bound, pre_operation_size_undercharges,
'                  summed_size_undercharges).
' Palette:  scheduling = control amber · charges = gate teal · prepare mutations = process lilac
'           publish = pool green · abort = surface coral · notes = note green / note indigo
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/replay-authority-charge-sizes.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh replay-authority-charge-sizes.puml)

@startuml replay-authority-charge-sizes
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_control
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #333333
title Replay authority charge sizes for one publication (DR-79)

start
:native session driver runs one intent at a time
(every intent carries footprint key [2, 0], so each frontier is one component); <<$ca_control>>
:**prepare** takes the authority lock; <<$ca_process>>
:identity lookups in pending_stack_event_ids, pending_replay_events, events
3 visits at <latex>\max(|S|, |P|, |E|)</latex> (searched at once); <<$ca_gate>>
:only when the allocation is enforced: the dominance scan,
<latex>|R|</latex> visits at <latex>|A|</latex>; <<$ca_gate>>
if (granted COMM with a debit of <latex>k</latex> lanes?) then (yes)
  :ledger visits for each lane: 2 + 9 + 4
  at <latex>L = \max(|R|, |Z|) + k</latex>, and at least <latex>|A|</latex> when the allocation is enforced; <<$ca_gate>>
  :event-map visits: 3 + 1, with 2 inserts
  at <latex>\max(|P|, |E|) + 1</latex>; <<$ca_gate>>
  :validate, add the debit to R, insert into P; <<$ca_process>>
else (no: denied COMM)
  :frontier insert: 1 visit at <latex>|F| + 1</latex>; <<$ca_gate>>
endif
note right
  Every charge is reserved before the first mutation.
  No .await separates prepare from publish, and the driver
  runs no other intent and no participant in between.
end note
if (operation completes?) then (publish)
  :remove from P, add the debit to Z,
  insert into E (or into F for a denied COMM); <<$ca_pool>>
else (abort)
  :remove from P, subtract the debit from R; <<$ca_surface>>
endif
:each search ran on a map no larger than its charged size
<latex>\Rightarrow</latex> at most <latex>11 \cdot h(n)</latex> comparisons and <latex>h(n)</latex> nodes (search_within_bound); <<$ca_note_green>>
stop

legend right
  S = pending stack identities, P = pending replay events, E = events,
  F = frontier, R = reserved, Z = realized, A = allocation, k = debit lanes.
  Pre-operation sizes and one bound on summed sizes undercharge
  (pre_operation_size_undercharges, summed_size_undercharges).
endlegend
@enduml
